  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "Originating in Oregon from a seedling of 'Azuma murasaki', this lovely variegated cultivar has the cascading shoots and semipendulous habit of 'Omure yama'. The deeply divided leaves have fingerlike lobes with crinkled edges. The new leaves emerge in the spring colored rose with pink tinges, becoming creamy white with green veins and margins for the summer. 'Tiger Rose' reaches 10 ft. (3 m) tall in 10 years and spreads 4 ft. (1.3 m) wide."
  },
